        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Animals: birds, common ostrich\n- Places: worldwide, Africa\n- Concepts: size range, flightlessness, taxonomy\n\nFacts:\n- Birds live worldwide.\n- Birds range in size from the 5 cm bee hummingbird to the 2.75 m ostrich.\n- The common ostrich, also called the ostrich, has the scientific name Struthio camelus.\n- The common ostrich is a large flightless bird native to Africa.\n- The common ostrich is the only living member, or one of two living members, of the genus Struthio in the ratite family.",
